{"builder":"Goal: one pull request for https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7 (padLeft for invoice numbers) that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n1. index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\n2. padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\n3. README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\n4. npm test passes\n\nSteps:\n1. Read index.js, README.md, package.json and test/strutil.test.js. The package is an ES module (\"type\": \"module\"), and tests run with `node --test`.\n2. In index.js, add and export `padLeft(s, width, fill = ' ')`, written in the same style as the existing functions (a one-line /** */ doc comment). It returns s padded on the left with fill until it is width characters long, e.g. padLeft('42', 5, '0') === '00042' and padLeft('42', 5) === '   42'. When s.length >= width it returns s unchanged. `s.padStart(width, fill)` does both.\n3. In README.md, add a `## padLeft(s, width, fill)` section that describes it, in the style of the existing sections. Important: README.md has no section for `slugify` at the moment, even though index.js exports it. Acceptance line 3 needs a section for EVERY exported function, so also add a `## slugify(s)` section (lower case, words joined by dashes). When you are done, README.md must have a `## name(...)` heading for each of capitalize, slugify, truncate and padLeft. Keep the Tests section at the end.\n4. In test/strutil.test.js, import padLeft and add tests for zero padding ('42',5,'0' -> '00042'), the default space fill ('42',5 -> '   42'), and the unchanged cases (length equal to width, and longer than width).\n5. Run `npm test` and make sure it passes with 0 failures. Then commit and open the pull request, and reference issue #7 in it.","verifier":"Check the PR head for issue https://github.com/o/strutil/issues/7. Run every command from the repository root at the PR head. Run `npm install` first only if package.json now lists dependencies. There is one check per acceptance line, in order.\n\nCheck 1. Expect: \"index.js exports padLeft(s, width, fill), which pads s on the left with fill (a space when fill is not given) to width characters\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; const p=m.padLeft; if(typeof p!=='function'){console.log('FAIL: padLeft not exported');process.exit(1)} const c=[[p('42',5,'0'),'00042'],[p('42',5),'   42'],[p('',3,'x'),'xxx'],[p('7',2,'0'),'07']]; let ok=true; for(const [a,b] of c){console.log(JSON.stringify(a),JSON.stringify(b),a===b); ok=ok&&a===b} console.log(ok?'PASS':'FAIL')\"\nAlso open index.js and confirm that padLeft is an exported function whose parameters are (s, width, fill), in that order.\nPASS: the last line printed is PASS, and index.js exports padLeft with parameters s, width, fill.\nFAIL: it prints FAIL (or 'FAIL: padLeft not exported'), it throws, or the exported signature is not padLeft(s, width, fill).\n\nCheck 2. Expect: \"padLeft returns s unchanged when s is already width characters or longer\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; const p=m.padLeft; if(typeof p!=='function'){console.log('FAIL: padLeft not exported');process.exit(1)} const c=[[p('abc',3,'0'),'abc'],[p('abcdef',3,'0'),'abcdef'],[p('abc',2),'abc'],[p('abc',0),'abc']]; let ok=true; for(const [a,b] of c){console.log(JSON.stringify(a),JSON.stringify(b),a===b); ok=ok&&a===b} console.log(ok?'PASS':'FAIL')\"\nPASS: the last line printed is PASS.\nFAIL: it prints FAIL, or it throws.\n\nCheck 3. Expect: \"README.md has a section for every function index.js exports\"\nRun:\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import * as m from './index.js'; import fs from 'node:fs'; const r=fs.readFileSync('README.md','utf8'); const fns=Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function'); const miss=fns.filter(f=>!new RegExp('^#{2,}\\\\s+\\`?'+f+'\\\\b','m').test(r)); console.log('exports:',fns.join(',')); console.log('missing:',miss.join(',')||'none'); console.log(miss.length?'FAIL':'PASS')\"\nThe script lists the exported functions and any that have no README heading (## or deeper) starting with the function's name. Before the change it reports slugify as missing, so slugify needs a section as well as padLeft. Read each section the script found and confirm it really describes that function.\nPASS: it prints 'missing: none' and PASS, and each of those sections describes its function.\nFAIL: any exported function is listed as missing, or a heading exists with no real description under it.\n\nCheck 4. Expect: \"npm test passes\"\nRun: npm test\nPASS: the command exits with code 0 and the summary shows '# fail 0'.\nFAIL: the exit code is not 0, or any test fails.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS/FAIL): see whether test/strutil.test.js now covers padLeft, including the default fill and the unchanged cases. Also note what padLeft does with a multi-character fill. Report these as notes only."}